-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  lex_strings_err_multichar.pcpp - Lexical: a character literal of several

  Break step of lex_strings: a character literal of several characters is
  PR0064, a warning, once each: it is the int32 its bytes make ('ab' is
  97 * 256 + 98). Past 4 characters it is too long for its type and keeps
  the last 4, still one report.
*******************************************************************************/

module exe lex_strings_err_multichar;

/*
  @@test
    kind run
    expect
    | 24930
    | 1650680933
    | [Heap] Allocs: 0, Frees: 0, Leaked: 0
  @@end
*/

begin
  println("{}", 'ab'); // WARN PR0064@17: character literal: multi-character character constant
  println("{}", 'abcde'); // WARN PR0064@17: character literal: character constant too long for its type
end.
